 "sheet_text": [
  "PROBLEMS (Shawn 2026-11-20: \"\u5bfc\u8f68\u5012\u662f\u53ef\u4ee5 ... \u770b\u770b\u80fd\u4e0d\u80fd\u628a\u5b83\u5bf9\u51c6\u5750\u4e0b\u53bb\") AND THE FEATURE THAT ANSWERS EACH",
  "1  Robot sits down off to one side: a pad misses its leaf (leaves alone take about +-6 mm)  ->  F1 two side guide rails beside the",
  "   backpack's lower tier: vertical guide face to z 12.5, 60 deg lead-in to z 24, 3 mm play per side, only beside the pads (x -77..-59)",
  "2  Robot sits down too far forward or back: the 8.7 mm pad misses the leaf tip  ->  F2 datum moved 3 mm forward (stop face and",
  "   leaves), so the falling tail always meets the stop; leaves a further 2.5 mm forward of the stop (sim seat is 1.9 deg nose-up)",
  "3  Robot too far back lands on the stop wall's relief ledge (z 14.6) or the tower top (z 22) and hangs  ->  F3 45 deg rear",
  "   lead-in from the stop face's top edge over the stop wall and the tower's side walls (replaces the screw-head relief ledge)",
  "4  Rails must not touch legs or feet in stand, sit and stand-up  ->  F4 rails end 8 mm behind where the left foot comes down at",
  "   the end of the stand-up (x -51), stay below z 24 and inside |y| 41; the legs never come behind x -40 while standing or sitting",
  "5  Dock stays put: unchanged, foam tape or Dual Lock under the (larger) plate.  One printed PLA part, no flexure, nothing to buy.",
  "",
  "MEASURED IN MUJOCO (real Brain sit, --model asbuilt --manifest current, --volt 7.6 --drop 0.036, 2 seeds; start offset = robot",
  "standing that far off; pass = both pads over their own leaf tip with 0.5 mm x margin and 1 mm y overlap, leaf pressed >= 1 mm,",
  "no short, no fall, no rail contact with any other robot part)",
  "   released A1:          x fails at 0   y fails at 0   yaw fails at 0",
  "   F2+F3, no rails:      x -6 .. +3 mm   y -3 .. +0 mm   yaw -5 .. +10 deg",
  "   F1+F2+F3 (drawn):     x -9 .. +3 mm   y -15 .. +3 mm   yaw -5 .. +5 deg",
  "   5-seed recheck of F1+F2+F3: y +3 mm fails 3 of 5 seeds (backpack hangs, pads lifted), so the dependable y window is -15..0 mm;",
  "   x -6 fails 1 of 5; combined x and y offsets of 6 and 9 mm fail; mu 0.2 and 0.5 rail friction each fail some cases",
  "   combo: 14/20 pass",
  "   friction: 7/11 pass",
  "   seeds: 11/15 pass",
  "   Rails clear legs and feet by >= 7 mm in stand, sit and rise; AFTER the stand-up the sim robot steps back onto the rails (-4 mm)",
  "",
  "WHAT THE SIM SHOWED ABOUT THE SIT: the tail drops 59 mm and moves 68 mm backward in 0.55 s, swinging up to 16 mm left and 16 deg",
  "while high, within 4 mm of its end point below z 19; the robot lands on its shins, feet lift; sideways push turns the robot about",
  "its knees (about 0.6 deg of yaw per mm); from +3 mm to the left the yawed backpack hangs at z 14.5 (pads lifted), the main limit."
 ]
